From: REG-Linux <dev@reglinux.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] efi_gop: normalize pitch to match offscreen buffer stride

On Qualcomm ABL UEFI, pixels_per_scan_line is aligned to 64 pixels
(e.g. 1088 for a 1080-pixel-wide panel). grub_video_gop_fill_mode_info()
sets mode_info.pitch = pixels_per_scan_line * bpp, which is larger than
width * bpp. However, the offscreen buffer is allocated as
width * height * sizeof(BLT_PIXEL) with no scan-line padding, and
gop->blt() is called with stride = mode_info.width * 4 (no padding).

This mismatch causes the render target to write row y at offset
y * pitch (padded), while gop->blt() reads row y at offset
y * (width * 4) (unpadded), producing a fine horizontal stripe
pattern on the display.

Fix: after grub_video_gop_fill_mode_info(), normalize pitch to
width * bytes_per_pixel so the render target and gop->blt() use the
same row stride as the allocated offscreen buffer.

Signed-off-by: REG-Linux <dev@reglinux.org>
---
 grub-core/video/efi_gop.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/grub-core/video/efi_gop.c b/grub-core/video/efi_gop.c
--- a/grub-core/video/efi_gop.c
+++ b/grub-core/video/efi_gop.c
@@ -469,6 +469,12 @@ grub_video_gop_setup (unsigned int width, unsigned int height,
   grub_video_gop_fill_mode_info (gop->mode->mode, info,
 				 &framebuffer.mode_info);
 
+  /* Normalize pitch to match offscreen buffer stride.  The offscreen buffer
+     is allocated as width*height with no scan-line padding, and gop->blt()
+     uses width*bytes_per_pixel as the source stride.  Force pitch to match.  */
+  framebuffer.mode_info.pitch = framebuffer.mode_info.width
+    * (framebuffer.mode_info.bpp / 8);
+
   framebuffer.ptr = (void *) (grub_addr_t) gop->mode->fb_base;
   framebuffer.offscreen
     = grub_malloc (framebuffer.mode_info.height
